{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-totaro-case}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:651e60937440f58917046ebf4f4d6f69118ff5273d17afca8b6ec7cf340bd3f2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f3f2e0b8dbaf90fd2ea6151f7f366b9f5c3e9f5f5bbca03445a26befe5be8a7a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack which is reduced and quasi-separated\nand whose associated topological space <MATH_0002> is irreducible.\nThen <MATH_0003> is integral.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ea37a2af728e653b972cfef5fcce01444e3c710d3caa93001bad190b2d3a5f32", "unit_id": "tag:0GWD:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta_\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-separated-decent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-quasi-compact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-integral-algebraic-stack}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a9b2d3a4efc40bf5360f999f30f8170414528e282079c5dfaa8cd108a669f74d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:91f0578dbc3fac479b03fcc624e6065ba9ae2988d1ac29c2e057c3b89782e30b", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is quasi-separated, then <MATH_0002> is decent\nby Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is quasi-separated, then\n<MATH_0004> is quasi-compact,\nhence <MATH_0005> is quasi-compact\nas the base change of <MATH_0006> by <MATH_0007>, see\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThus we see that all the hypotheses of\nDefinition <REF_0003> hold\n(and we also see that we may replace ``quasi-separated'' by\n``<MATH_0008> is quasi-compact'').\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b074ae09591bbbab5a0a5258bfa2a7c104da3411f0ef1955d816ebe032f1e39b", "unit_id": "tag:0GWD:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\overline{\\{x\\}}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0010": "$|\\mathcal{Z}|$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-decent-irreducible-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e573a0d1f183a2a838e8aaba605993eabff3b519e26137c0569c49df67cdbe75", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6e93db23c89cc6f6dda82897e537f976c20ff1dcfceef36dbb01c150ef182808", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a decent algebraic stack such that\n<MATH_0002> is quasi-compact.\nThere are canonical bijections between the following sets:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the set of points of <MATH_0003>, i.e., <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0003> the set of irreducible closed subsets of <MATH_0005>,\n<STRUCT_0004> the set of integral closed substacks of <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThe bijection from (1) to (2) sends <MATH_0007> to <MATH_0008>.\nThe bijection from (3) to (2) sends <MATH_0009> to <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:21cab532ebc9038a9edc53ea9bc3c08c329cf740dea5e2fc39c764b565ac3d61", "unit_id": "tag:0GWE:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GWA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\subset |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{Z}| = T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0006": "$T$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0011": "$|\\mathcal{Z}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-decent-sober}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-definition-reduced-induced-stack}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-representable-decent}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-monomorphism-cartesian-square-inertia}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:941a24d037c40f698082c751f9890f340f964ffa01a9fea283505d51a22dd690", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7c9fd2ae1cffef376b9fe48fe7f590d498d84a94856f65a156a4445026608fb2", "source_text": "Our map defines a bijection between (1) and (2) as <MATH_0001> is\nsober by  Proposition <REF_0001>.\nGiven <MATH_0002> closed and irreducible, there is a\nunique reduced closed substack <MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004>, namely, <MATH_0005>\nis the reduced induced subspace structure on <MATH_0006>, see\nProperties of Stacks, Definition\n<REF_0002>.\nThen <MATH_0007> is an integral algebraic stack because it is\ndecent (Lemma <REF_0003>), the\nmorphism <MATH_0008> is quasi-compact\n(as the base change of <MATH_0009>, see\nLemma <REF_0004>),\n<MATH_0010> is reduced, and <MATH_0011> is irreducible.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b5370c4d336c3c1c3e61d6e7761b1eeeb40c9e9c645f21062eea161445ecb86", "unit_id": "tag:0GWE:proof"}
